{
  "Title": "ELSA-2026-97585:  bind9.18 security, bug fix, and enhancement update (MODERATE)",
  "Description": "[32:9.18.29-28]\n- Prevent assertion failure in dns64 mode with break-dnssec yes (CVE-2026-19666)\n- Prevent memory leak on following HTTPS/SVCB RR (CVE-2026-81563)\n- Prevent crash on wildcard responses containing both NSEC and NSEC3 proofs (CVE-2026-80274)\n- Reject oversized negative cached records early (CVE-2026-19667)\n- Set limit to following HTTPS/SVCB aliases (CVE-2026-81736)\n\n[32:9.18.29-27]\n- Rebuild to become part of regular release\n\n[32:9.18.29-26]\n- Add new root key 38696 into package files (RHEL-131887)\n- Update built-in anchors in delv and named\n\n[32:9.18.29-25]\n- Remove downstream introduced double-free (CVE-2026-5950)\n\n[32:9.18.29-24]\n- Avoid unbounded recursion loop (CVE-2026-5950)\n- Limit overlapping addresses resolver usage (CVE-2026-3592)\n\n[32:9.18.29-23]\n- Fix NSEC3 signer validation (CVE-2026-10723)\n\n[32:9.18.29-22]\n- Reject out-of-zone NSEC next owner names (CVE-2026-13321)\n\n[32:9.18.29-21]\n- Fix cache exhaustion via dns_slabheaders (CVE-2026-11622)\n\n[32:9.18.29-20]\n- Reject invalid signed wildcard records (CVE-2026-11721)\n\n[32:9.18.29-19]\n- Fix RPZ wildcard expansion self-referential CNAME (CVE-2026-11331)",
  "Platform": [
    "Oracle Linux 9"
  ],
